## TIẾNG ANH · 16:30–17:00 — Thứ Ba: Giải thích khái niệm

**Chủ đề: một database riêng cho mỗi pull request.**

> *"The thing I set up today that I'm most pleased with: every pull request gets its own database.*
> *Neon supports branching — you branch a database the way you branch Git, and it takes about a second. So the CI job creates a branch named after the PR, runs migrations against it, runs the integration suite, and deletes it when the PR closes.*
> *Three things that gives me. Tests run against real Postgres, so real constraints and real transaction behavior — a mocked database can't catch a bug where I forgot a unique constraint. Concurrent PRs don't interfere. And most importantly, every migration gets applied from scratch on every PR, so a broken migration fails in review instead of in production.*
> *That last one matters because migrations are the most dangerous change you can make on a backend. On mobile a bad deploy means a crash. On the backend it can mean permanent data loss.*
> *I also deliberately broke CI four different ways to check each gate actually catches what it's supposed to. One of them didn't."*

Câu cuối là câu hay nhất — nó cho thấy bạn kiểm chứng chứ không giả định.

**5 từ mới:**

| Từ / cụm | Nghĩa | Câu mẫu |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `branch a database` | tạo nhánh database | *You branch a database the way you branch Git.* |
| `interfere` (v) | giẫm lên nhau | *Concurrent PRs don't interfere.* |
| `from scratch` | từ đầu, từ số không | *Every migration is applied from scratch.* |
| `fail in review` | rớt ở khâu review | *A broken migration fails in review.* |
| `deliberately break` | cố tình làm hỏng | *I deliberately broke CI four ways.* |

